results/*
!results/*.json

# ⭐ Except the determinism intermediates, which are scratch, not artefacts.
#
# ⛔ This line must live **here**, not in the root `.gitignore`. The negation
# above force-includes every JSON under `results/`, and a pattern in a deeper
# `.gitignore` beats the root's — so the root rule silently did nothing. That
# cost a debugging round.
#
# It matters because `run.sh publish` writes these two *while* producing the
# record: untracked, they make the tree dirty during the run, `git_dirty` is
# stamped true, and `mkfigs.py` refuses the output. The publish path could not
# emit a publishable record until this existed.
results/.determinism-*.json

# ⛔ And their CURRENT name. `run.sh` renamed the intermediates to
# `.<record-stem>-run<n>.json` so two publishes could not share scratch, and the
# line above silently stopped matching: every publish after the first on a box
# then stamped `git_dirty = true` and was refused. That is why two of the three
# local tier-4 records came out dirty. Found 2026-09-25 by reading `git status`
# on the WSL clone, not by anything failing.
results/.*-run[0-9].json

upstream/log/
